  "analysis": "The patient's presentation of pancytopenia (low hemoglobin, leukocyte, and platelet counts) along with a hypocellular bone marrow on biopsy points towards aplastic anemia. Aplastic anemia is characterized by bone marrow failure resulting in peripheral blood cytopenias. The absence of an abnormal cell population in the bone marrow biopsy supports this diagnosis. Other differentials like myelodysplastic syndrome and acute lymphocytic leukemia typically show dysplastic or abnormal cell populations in the bone marrow. Infectious mononucleosis is less likely given the chronicity of symptoms and lack of typical findings. Drug-induced immune pancytopenia would usually involve a history of recent drug exposure, which is not mentioned in the case. Therefore, the most likely diagnosis in this patient is aplastic anemia.",
